parameters.description:
List of features. You can specify up to 50 items in one request. The format is as follows:

- **functionName** (required): Name of the feature. For supported features, see [Feature list](~~388460~~). Separate multiple parameters with commas (,).

- **argName** (required): Configuration item for **functionName**. You can specify multiple configuration items.

- **argValue** (required): Value for the configuration item of **functionName**.

- **parentid** (optional): ID of a rule condition. By configuring the **condition** function (rules engine) in [Domain configuration feature parameters](~~388460~~), you can create rule conditions that match and filter user requests based on parameters in the request. Each rule condition generates a [configid](~~388994~~) after creation. This configid can be used as a ParentId parameter referenced by other feature functions, enabling flexible combinations of rule conditions and feature configurations.

If **parentId** is set to **-1**, the existing rule condition for this configuration is deleted.

```[{
   "functionArgs": [{
     "argName": "Feature parameter A", 
     "argValue": "Value for Feature parameter A"
    }, 
  {
    "argName": "Feature parameter B", 
    "argValue": "Value for Feature parameter B"
     }], 
 "functionName": "Feature name",
 "parentId": Optional. ConfigId of the referenced rule condition
}]
```

Example without using **parentId**:
To add an origin HTTP request header using the **origin\_request\_header** function, use the following request parameters:

```[{
        "functionArgs": [{
            "argName": "header_operation_type",
            "argValue": "add"
        }, {
            "argName": "header_name",
            "argValue": "Accept-Encoding"
        }, {
            "argName": "header_value",
            "argValue": "gzip"
        }, {
            "argName": "duplicate",
            "argValue": "off"
        }],
        "functionName": "origin_request_header"
}]
```

Example using **parentId**:
To add an origin HTTP request header using the **origin\_request\_header** function and reference a rule condition with **configid=222728944812032**, use the following request parameters:

```[{
        "functionArgs": [{
            "argName": "header_operation_type",
            "argValue": "add"
        }, {
            "argName": "header_name",
            "argValue": "Accept-Encoding"
        }, {
            "argName": "header_value",
            "argValue": "gzip"
        }, {
            "argName": "duplicate",
            "argValue": "off"
        }],
        "functionName": "origin_request_header",
        "parentId": 222728944812032
}]
```

Example to remove a **parentId** reference from an existing configuration:
The **origin\_request\_header** function currently references a rule condition with **configid=222728944812032**. To remove this reference, use the following request parameters:

```[{
        "functionArgs": [{
            "argName": "header_operation_type",
            "argValue": "add"
        }, {
            "argName": "header_name",
            "argValue": "Accept-Encoding"
        }, {
            "argName": "header_value",
            "argValue": "gzip"
        }, {
            "argName": "duplicate",
            "argValue": "off"
        }],
        "functionName": "origin_request_header",
        "parentId": -1
}]
```
